W: 1. My life flows on in endless song;
W: Above earth's lamentations,
W: I hear the real, though far-off hymn
W: That hails a new creation;
W: Through all the tumult and the strife,
W: I hear its music ringing;
W: It sounds an echo in my soul;
W: How can I keep from singing?
W:
W: 2. Although the tempest loudly roars,
W: I hear the truth, it liveth.
W: But though the darkness 'round me close,
W: Songs in the night it giveth.
W: No storm can shake my inmost calm
W: While to that rock I'm clinging;
W: Since love is lord of heaven and earth,
W: How can I keep from singing?
W:
W: 3. When tyrants tremble, sick with fear,
W: And hear their death-knell ringing,
W: When friends rejoice both far and near,
W: How can I keep from singing?
W: In prison cell and dungeon vile,
W: Our thoughts to them are winging;
W: When friends by shame are undefiled,
W: How can I keep from singing?
%
